<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="ad15059b">&lt;p&gt;
    Defining the case for change and change vision includes:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conducting interviews or workshops with the program leadership team and a cross-section of stakeholders/ and other
        relevant individuals involved in the program delivery to solicit their perspective on best ways to articulate the
        change vision and what the business solution will do for the business.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identifying the program’s strategic intent to inform the change vision and compelling case for change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Sharing the change vision and case for change with the program team before communicating to affected stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Capturing feedback from change vision and case for change activities and consolidate this into lessons
        learned&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="4f21db51"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="723ec383"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="f17dd0b1"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="7906e60">To articulate, for stakeholders, in an inspirational and motivating way, what the change initiative intends to achieve, how
it will achieve it and why change needs to take place to build awareness and cultivate a sense of urgency.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="ccaf3328"></attribute>
